  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py`. It gives each part `cents // parts` and adds one extra cent to each of the first `cents % parts` parts. If `parts` is below 1, it raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe new tests are in `tests/test_money.py`. They cover an even split, the remainder going to the first parts (`split(101, 3)` gives `[34, 34, 33]`), the parts summing to `cents`, and `parts=0` raising. The full suite passes (10 tests).\n\nI didn't special-case negative `cents`. With Python's floor division, `split(-100, 3)` gives `[-33, -33, -34]`, so the extra cent lands on the last parts rather than the first.",
